{"title":"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems\">2002 AMC 12P #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">2002 AMC 10P #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is a perfect square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/9838e2c50c357580dc586faa4b02fe9855392a51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }4^4 5^5 6^6 \\qquad \\text{(B) }4^4 5^6 6^5 \\qquad \\text{(C) }4^5 5^4 6^6 \\qquad \\text{(D) }4^6 5^4 6^5 \\qquad \\text{(E) }4^6 5^5 6^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"535\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer to be a perfect square, all the primes in its prime factorization must have an even exponent. With a quick glance at the answer choices, we can eliminate options\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1baff6050db5d3e78ff320d0358d74adf9b153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> is an odd power\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9ba1d2dfb67b209df390d7fdeed8a2caa4916f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^5 = 2^5 \\cdot 3^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef89940c9d0d4b76ae12725c459ab738decd42d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^5$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is an odd power\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9ba1d2dfb67b209df390d7fdeed8a2caa4916f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^5 = 2^5 \\cdot 3^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef89940c9d0d4b76ae12725c459ab738decd42d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^5$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is an odd power, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1baff6050db5d3e78ff320d0358d74adf9b153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> is an odd power.\n</p><p>This leaves option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0177d15168f7b1af172ddb1ebd4ae8d56b1aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/985c0b965030ca99f64448b25c4f343a9eb2c6f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^5=(2^{2})^{5}=2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"21\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2cc331fc133b06d4a311a155b18cf258daa91b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10, 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are all even, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is a perfect square. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093bc33a7685b916df7f8b8f1225d3b81a288c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 4^5 5^4 6^6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"103\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P\">2002 AMC 10P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Re